          "text": "{\"target_translation\":\"I love you.\",\"dimensions\":{\"T\":{\"score\":4,\"evidence_status\":\"assessable\",\"confidence\":0.99,\"reason\":\"Nikki directly avows love as her present emotional state. The narration explicitly characterizes the exchange as an honest admission, making truth-state presentation the expression’s dominant force.\",\"evidence\":[{\"block_id\":\"target\",\"quotation\":\"I love you\"},{\"block_id\":\"scene\",\"quotation\":\"She turned to him, her heart full. “I love you,” she said suddenly\"},{\"block_id\":\"scene\",\"quotation\":\"The admission felt like a release, a moment of pure honesty\"}]},\"P\":{\"score\":0,\"evidence_status\":\"assessable\",\"confidence\":0.95,\"reason\":\"The focal expression contains no promise, proposal, or undertaking by Nikki to maintain the relationship or perform a future action. Keith’s reciprocation and their continuing intimacy acknowledge the avowal but do not convert Nikki’s words into a commitment.\",\"evidence\":[{\"block_id\":\"target\",\"quotation\":\"I love you\"},{\"block_id\":\"scene\",\"quotation\":\"Keith stilled, then smiled. “I love you too,” he said\"}]},\"E\":{\"score\":3,\"evidence_status\":\"assessable\",\"confidence\":0.94,\"reason\":\"In addition to avowing love, the expression is represented as a spontaneous affective outpouring: it is said suddenly, escapes before Nikki can restrain it, and produces a sense of release. This substantially supports expressive-discharge force.\",\"evidence\":[{\"block_id\":\"scene\",\"quotation\":\"“I love you,” she said suddenly, the words spilling out before she could stop them.\"},{\"block_id\":\"scene\",\"quotation\":\"The admission felt like a release\"}]},\"O\":{\"score\":0,\"evidence_status\":\"assessable\",\"confidence\":0.94,\"reason\":\"The focal expression’s core force is adequately captured by avowal and spontaneous expressive discharge. No distinct residual function, such as a request, command, greeting, or conventional act, is supported.\",\"evidence\":[{\"block_id\":\"target\",\"quotation\":\"I love you\"}]}},\"original_speech_situation\":\"Nikki says this to Keith while they are lying in bed after an intimate encounter, with the narration describing her heart as full. Her declaration is sudden and unplanned; Keith pauses, smiles, and reciprocates it steadily and sincerely.\",\"affection_evidence\":\"present\",\"undertaking_and_uptake\":\"Nikki undertakes no identifiable obligation in the focal expression. Keith receives the avowal positively and reciprocates with “I love you too,” after which they kiss. This establishes mutual acknowledgment, not agreed commitment terms.\",\"recognised_work\":false,\"recognition_note\":\"I do not recognize the supplied passages as a specific known work.\",\"limitations\":\"The supplied scene strongly supports affection and spontaneous honesty at this moment, but it does not establish the durability of Nikki’s feelings or any defined future commitment. The much later material involving Franco lacks the intervening context needed to determine what happened to Nikki and Keith’s relationship and does not negate the original avowal’s force.\"}"
